**Theorem 7.1 (same-version finite completed-frame induction).** Assume
actual finite supply of each reached canonical frame/code remainder and
reached-local progress of the original finite source/channel primitives.
Every reached lawful $D_2$ fragment has finite completion to its annotated
Ready. Every acquisition-or-later cut can subsequently be covered and
selected, with a communicated/acquired target, and called on this same
fixed-H version. Earlier converter and registry microcuts are included.

Proof. Installation is Proposition 2.4. Induct on completed installed
frames. An original source frame terminates by LJA Theorem 4.5 and its
literal RD/MR adapter. Cover's Boundary stops at the actual predecessor
Ready, now after registry work and common return. That predecessor is
finite by induction. Prefix has its actual finite countdown. The Step
proof in Theorem 4.4 interprets earlier computations one native row at a
time. It does not need to solve a represented semantic recovery afresh.
Next and Select use immutable earlier covers; Issue and Call have fixed
selected targets. A direct Convert has an earlier completed input and
finite target/body lists. Its validation and cycle terminate by Theorem
5.7, and Publish, registry update and return by the finite scan/assignment
proofs. Typed negative results have the same finite return.

No newly admitted frame can select an in-progress output of itself.
Thus dependencies of every successful input lie in completed predecessors,
and the induction has no current-service self-reference. An unfinished
canonical ingress has a finite canonical extension by definition. At other
cuts follow the reached fragment; an installation cut completes its actual
installation. A later Cover freezes the predecessor containing that cut.
RCA's real Next enumeration acquires its directory entry, or Select uses
an actually acquired unary choice. The immutable package target is not
replaced by the later live meter. A common later cover by itself does not
identify an uncommunicated intended cut. These are the unchanged acquired
selection conditions of RCA Theorem 3.3. ∎

